T(-78.6386 35.7721)","signal.location.radius":"30000","filter.exclude.entities":"9A5680C3-D7D9-4740-8B09-B67B02EBFFCC","filter.popularity.max":"0.93","take":"8"},"ms":15527,"count":8,"mode":"live"},{"path":"/v2/insights","params":{"filter.type":"urn:entity:place","filter.location":"POINT(-75.1636 39.9524)","filter.location.radius":"30000","filter.tags":"urn:tag:category:place:live_music_venue","signal.interests.entities":"9A5680C3-D7D9-4740-8B09-B67B02EBFFCC","signal.demographics.age":"25_to_29","take":"8"},"ms":15952,"count":8,"mode":"live"}],"baseline":[{"label":"Asheville, NC","lat":35.6009,"lon":-82.554},{"label":"Knoxville, TN","lat":35.9606,"lon":-83.9207},{"label":"Nashville, TN","lat":36.1659,"lon":-86.7844},{"label":"Atlanta, GA","lat":33.749,"lon":-84.388},{"label":"Charlotte, NC","lat":35.2271,"lon":-80.8431}],"baselineUnmatched":[],"baselineChecks":{"legsOver":0,"longestLeg":5.4,"totalDrive":16.2,"radiusConflicts":0},"home":{"label":"Asheville, NC","lat":35.6009,"lon":-82.554},"plan":{"artist":"Wednesday","headline":"5 dates down and up the East Coast, where Wednesday's numbers are highest and they haven't played yet","summary":"Start at home in Asheville, head south to Atlanta and Savannah, then turn north through Raleigh, Richmond and Philadelphia. All five are in Qloo's top 20 for Wednesday out of 182 metros (affinity 0.932 to 0.974). No two stops are within 120 km of each other or of Chicago or NYC, and no drive is over 7 hours. The crowd skews 25 to 29 (+0.92) and female (+0.46), and under-24s under-index (-0.37), so 21+ clubs are fine. Florida scored well too, but it's too far to fit in this run.","stops":[{"city":"Atlanta, GA","lat":33.749,"lon":-84.388,"why":"Affinity 0.953, rank 0.846, in a 2M metro. Shortest drive of the run, 3.9 hours from Asheville, so it's an easy first night.","affinity":0.953,"venue":{"name":"Variety Playhouse","why":"Historic, casual neighborhood room in Little Five Points (affinity 0.834, popularity 0.998). A standing crowd suits the loud set better than a seated listening room.","alternates":["The EARL","The Drunken Unicorn","Eddie's Attic"]},"openers":[{"name":"Mattiel","why":"0.945 affinity in Atlanta and a local draw. Garage/psych energy fits the night."},{"name":"Vagabon","why":"0.948 here, one of the highest opener scores in this city."}],"promo":{"angle":"East Atlanta / Little Five crowd. Use the EARL and the Star Bar for flyers. Entireworld (0.949) is the top brand match here.","partners":["The EARL","The Star Community Bar","Entireworld","Costar"],"copy":"Atlanta, first night out. Variety Playhouse with Mattiel. Come early, it's a short drive for us and we'll be loud."},"driveHoursFromPrev":3.9,"date":"2027-03-04","weekday":"Thu","evidence":{"tasteRank":7,"of":182,"metroPop":2013096,"opportunity":0.09,"venueAffinity":0.834}},{"city":"Savannah, GA","lat":32.0835,"lon":-81.0998,"why":"Affinity 0.94, rank 0.821, in a 203k metro. Opportunity is +0.60, so taste here is far ahead of the city's size. It's the kind of mid-size market this run is built around.","affinity":0.94,"venue":{"name":"The Wormhole Neighborhood Pub & Music Venue","why":"Proper music bar on Bull St (affinity 0.845). It's small, and a sellout in a small room is the point here.","alternates":["Starland Yard","Moodright’s (21 & Up)"]},"openers":[{"name":"Becca Mancari","why":"0.944 in Savannah. Alt-country leaning, which matches that side of Wednesday."},{"name":"Whitmer Thomas","why":"0.941 here with low popularity (0.554), so a cheap, small opener."}],"promo":{"angle":"Small-city art-school crowd. Graveface Records is the obvious partner for an in-store or poster wall.","partners":["Graveface Records & Curiosities","The Sentient Bean","Entireworld"],"copy":"Savannah, we've wanted this one for a while. The Wormhole, small room, with Becca Mancari. Grab a ticket before it's gone."},"driveHoursFromPrev":5.3,"date":"2027-03-05","weekday":"Fri","evidence":{"tasteRank":14,"of":182,"metroPop":202779,"opportunity":0.6,"venueAffinity":0.845}},{"city":"Raleigh, NC","lat":35.7721,"lon":-78.6386,"why":"Affinity 0.971, rank 0.892, #5 in the region. Opportunity +0.19 with a 1.19M metro. It's a home-state crowd that hasn't had its own headline date.","affinity":0.971,"venue":{"name":"Lincoln Theatre","why":"Historic, casual, mid-size room downtown (affinity 0.81, popularity 0.997). It holds more than the Pour House if the date sells well.","alternates":["The Pour House Music Hall & Record Shop","Kings"]},"openers":[{"name":"Ratboys","why":"Top opener match in Raleigh at 0.953. Fans also over-index in every other city on this run."},{"name":"Moontype","why":"0.940 here. A smaller, dreamy guitar band and a cheap support slot."}],"promo":{"angle":"NC crowd. Lean on the record-store and indie-bar circuit around downtown and Hillsborough St.","partners":["Schoolkids Records","The Pour House Music Hall & Record Shop","Pitchfork","Bandcamp"],"copy":"Raleigh's a couple hours from home and we've never done our own night there. Fixing that at the Lincoln Theatre with Ratboys."},"driveHoursFromPrev":6.9,"date":"2027-03-06","weekday":"Sat","evidence":{"tasteRank":5,"of":182,"metroPop":1190669,"opportunity":0.19,"venueAffinity":0.81}},{"city":"Richmond, VA","lat":37.5538,"lon":-77.4603,"why":"Affinity 0.932, rank 0.815, in a 439k metro. Opportunity +0.31. The openers score high here too: Bartees Strange and Ratboys both 0.966.","affinity":0.932,"venue":{"name":"The Canal Club","why":"Historic warehouse club in the entertainment district (affinity 0.82, popularity 0.994). The right size for a headline night.","alternates":["The Camel","Gallery5","Fallout"]},"openers":[{"name":"Bartees Strange","why":"Highest opener affinity in Richmond at 0.966. A regional draw from the Mid-Atlantic."},{"name":"Buck Meek","why":"0.950 here. Americana and indie folk, which suits the country-leaning songs."}],"promo":{"angle":"Richmond's 25 to 29 bar crowd hangs out at The Camel and Gallery5. Run posters and pre-show events there.","partners":["The Camel","Gallery5","Bandcamp","Pitchfork"],"copy":"Richmond, first time headlining your town. Canal Club with Bartees Strange. See you there."},"driveHoursFromPrev":3.3,"date":"2027-03-07","weekday":"Sun","evidence":{"tasteRank":18,"of":182,"metroPop":439086,"opportunity":0.31,"venueAffinity":0.82}},{"city":"Philadelphia, PA","lat":39.9524,"lon":-75.1636,"why":"Highest-affinity metro we can route to: 0.974, Qloo rank 0.895. That's #4 in North America, ahead of NYC (0.944) and Chicago (0.948), both already played. The openers' fan numbers are highest here too (0.95 to 0.97).","affinity":0.974,"venue":{"name":"World Cafe Live","why":"Affinity 0.924, popularity 0.998. A proper concert hall with accessible seating, and a good size for a first Philly headline.","alternates":["Johnny Brenda's","Kung Fu Necktie","The Fillmore Philadelphia"]},"openers":[{"name":"Frances Quinlan","why":"0.960 affinity in Philly. It's her home scene, and the same introspective, lyric-first crowd."},{"name":"Pom Pom Squad","why":"0.955 affinity here. Brings a louder guitar set that matches Wednesday's heavier side."}],"promo":{"angle":"Philly's fans come from the indie-press and Bandcamp world. Lean on Pitchfork and Bandcamp, plus the Ortlieb's / Kung Fu Necktie bar scene for posters.","partners":["Bandcamp","Pitchfork","Ortlieb's","Crap Eyewear"],"copy":"Philly, we've been through on the way to other places too many times. This time we're stopping. World Cafe Live, with Frances Quinlan. Tickets Friday."},"driveHoursFromPrev":4.9,"date":"2027-03-08","weekday":"Mon","evidence":{"tasteRank":4,"of":182,"metroPop":3349673,"opportunity":0.05,"venueAffinity":0.924}}],"skipped":[{"city":"Asheville, NC","reason":"Home base and highest affinity (0.999), but it's the tour start and they've played it plenty of times. Johnson City (0.946) and Greenville (0.92) are within about 85 km of it, so we left those out too."},{"city":"Miami, FL","reason":"Affinity 0.99, but it's 1,116 km from home and can't connect to the rest of the route inside 7-hour legs. Same for Coral Springs (0.981) and West Palm Beach (0.969). Worth a separate Florida run."},{"city":"Charleston, SC","reason":"Affinity 0.93 and opportunity +0.36. Savannah scored higher (0.94 / +0.60) and fills the same southern slot. It's the backup if the Savannah to Raleigh drive gets too long."},{"city":"Wilmington, NC","reason":"Opportunity +0.68, but affinity is lower (0.926) and the venues are mostly beach bars and sports grills."},{"city":"Knoxville, TN","reason":"Affinity 0.921, 130 km from home. Too close to Asheville to be worth a date, and lower scores than the stops we picked."},{"city":"Baltimore, MD / Washington, DC","reason":"0.941 / 0.934, but Philly scores higher and gives a better route. Baltimore and DC are about 55 km apart, so we could only ever pick one."}],"risks":["Savannah to Raleigh is 469 km, 6.9 hours, just under the 7-hour limit. Traffic or weather could push it over. Charleston is the swap if needed (about 5 to 6 hours each side).","Philadelphia is about 130 km from NYC, which we already played. The route check didn't flag it, but read the NYC radius clause before confirming.","Savannah has only a few real music rooms. The Wormhole is the only proper club in the results, so book it early.","The EARL came up in Atlanta's bar/hangout list, not the venue list. Confirm the room size before pitching.","Ratboys scores high in every city. If you want one support act for the whole run, they're the pick, and the per-city openers above become local swaps.","Atlanta's highest-affinity room is Eddie's Attic (0.89), but it's a seated singer-songwriter room. We went with Variety Playhouse for a standing crowd."],"totalDriveHours":24.3,"startDate":"2027-03-04","checks":{"legsOver":0,"radiusConflicts":0},"mode":"live","model":"claude-opus-5-5"}}